Vacaturebeschrijving
   SummaryDo you have experience in metal work or are you interested in this sector? Start as a Production Worker in Venray! You will work in a 2-shift system, earn up to € 19,45 gross per hour including shift allowance, and get plenty of opportunities to learn, grow and develop yourself within this family-owned company.
About the jobAs a Production Worker, you will work in the metal industry. You will join a small and close team where you play an important role in the production process. Do you have experience in metal work and are you motivated to learn more about this type of work? Then this could be a great opportunity for you.
Your tasks include:
- Loading and unloading metal parts in CNC machines;
- Checking products with measuring tools to ensure the correct size and quality;
- Performing simple finishing work, such as grinding and removing sharp edges;
- Reporting any problems with products, machines or the production process.

As a Production Worker you will work in a fixed 2-shift schedule from Monday to Friday. One week you work from 06:00 to 14:30 and the next week from 14:30 to 23:00. On Fridays, the working hours are different: from 06:00 to 12:30 or from 12:30 to 19:00.
What we offer- A salary of € 17,36 to € 19,45 gross per hour including shift allowance;
- Travel allowance of € 0,23 per kilometer from 10km single distance;
- 27 vacation days and 8% holiday allowance;
- Pension from your first working day;
- Working within an international company with modern production technology;
- Opportunities to develop yourself within the company and responsibility;
- The possibility of a permanent contract when performing well.

What we ask- You speak the English of German language;
- You have experience in the metal industry or a similar production environment;
- You are motivated and willing to learn.

About the companyOur client is a manufacturing company and a family-owned business with a down-to-earth and informal working env

For our client in Kessel, we are looking for a production employee for the Maintenance and Laundry department. In this role, you’ll be responsible for inspecting used materials for quality, cleaning them, packaging, and getting them ready for transport or storage. You'll work with modern machinery to ensure the customer receives rental items that are complete, clean, and undamaged. You’ll be handling various tent components such as floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases, cleaning them both manually and with machines. Familiarity with industrial machinery and using a high-pressure cleaner is essential.

Your tasks will include:

- Washing and maintaining tent components and rental materials (e.g., floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases) by machine and hand;
- Operating industrial washers, dryers, high-pressure cleaners, and overhead cranes;
- Monitoring product quality and detecting any damages;
- Inspecting and packing canvases;
- Preparing materials for storage or transport;
- Maintaining a safe and sustainable workspace.

You will be working in an international environment where Dutch and English are the primary languages. Working hours are from 07:00 to 15:30, Monday through Friday.

We are seeking someone with experience in an industrial production setting and a hands-on approach. You’re not afraid to roll up your sleeves and tackle physical tasks. Additionally, you possess:

- A completed VMBO or basic vocational education (level 2) or an equivalent qualification;
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- A forklift certification, or you’re willing to obtain one;
- A desire to grow by participating in internal training opportunities.
